Rāvaṇa scorns Mālyavān as enemy prompted and pro Rāma --- Rāvaṇa vows never to bow nor return Sītā from fear --- Rāvaṇa boasts he will slay Rāma after the sea crossing --- Mālyavān falls silent and takes leave for home --- Rāvaṇa posts Prahasta and kinsmen at four gates --- Rāvaṇa stations Virūpākṣa centrally and enters his palace